  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given, maximum amplitude A<sub>max</sub> = 10 V<br /><br />Minimum amplitude A<sub>min</sub> = 2 V<br /><br />Let A<sub>c</sub> and A<sub>m</sub> be the amplitudes of carrier wave and signal wave<br /><br />∴&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A<sub>max</sub> = A<sub>c</sub> + A<sub>m</sub> = 10&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;...(i)<br /><br />and&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A<sub>min</sub> = A<sub>c</sub> – A<sub>m</sub> = 2 &nbsp;&nbsp;...(i)<br /><br />Adding the Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get<br /><br />2A<sub>c</sub> = 12<br /><br />or&nbsp;&nbsp;A<sub>c</sub> = 6 V<br /><br />and&nbsp;&nbsp;A<sub>m</sub> = 10 – 6 = 4 V</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
